From: Benik3 <benik333@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 01:53:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: jz: report read CRC errors the loop did not see

jz_mmc_send_cmd checks MSC_STAT_CRC_READ_ERROR only at the top of its
read loop, which it reaches only when the RX FIFO has run empty, and it
leaves the loop as soon as DATA_TRAN_DONE is set. The CRC error of the
last block comes with DATA_TRAN_DONE, so it was never seen. When the
card fills the FIFO faster than the CPU empties it, as in 4-bit high
speed mode, the loop does not get back to the top during the transfer
at all, and a CRC error in any block was missed. Corrupt data then
reached the caller as a good read.

CRC_READ_ERROR stays set until the next command, so one check after
DATA_TRAN_DONE catches an error in any block. On a model of the
controller, a last-block error and a mid-transfer error with a full
FIFO both came back as success before this change and as COMM_ERR
after it; clean reads are unchanged.

The SPL copy of the loop is not changed: it only runs when booting from
an SD card.

Signed-off-by: Benik3 <benik333@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/mmc/jz_mmc.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/jz_mmc.c b/drivers/mmc/jz_mmc.c
--- a/drivers/mmc/jz_mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/jz_mmc.c
@@ -185,6 +185,9 @@
 		} while (!(stat & MSC_STAT_DATA_TRAN_DONE));
 		while (!(jz_mmc_readl(priv, MSC_IFLG) & MSC_IREG_DATA_TRAN_DONE));
 		jz_mmc_writel(MSC_IREG_DATA_TRAN_DONE, priv, MSC_IFLG);
+		/* the loop sees CRC errors only when the FIFO runs empty */
+		if (jz_mmc_readl(priv, MSC_STAT) & MSC_STAT_CRC_READ_ERROR)
+			return COMM_ERR;
 	}
 #else
 	if (data && (data->flags & MMC_DATA_READ)) {
